&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; In all the places where SCP-5986 specimens have been found, a wall is to be built around them, restricting access from the public. Places where SCP-XXXX can grow are to be monitored daily by MTF Theta-4 (“Gardeners”) for specimens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5986 is a species of plant, known to the public as &lt;em&gt;Artica flora&lt;/em&gt;. Massive data about SCP-5986 is known to the public due to it having a similar appearance to &lt;em&gt;Bellis perris&lt;/em&gt;&lt;sup class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;&gt;&lt;a id=&quot;footnoteref-30912-1&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot; class=&quot;footnoteref&quot;  &gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/sup&gt; and it being found by Canadians. SCP-5986 can only grow in areas with a temperature of less than, or equal to, 4°C.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SCP-5986 possesses multiple anomalous abilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to produce seeds, seemingly forever, leading to mass population&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to drop the temperature around it down to up to -53°C&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to launch it’s seeds with distances up to 500 meters at rates of 102 mph&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to make the surrounding area pile up with up to 60&amp;#160;cm of snow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to survive on any solid object, as long as it’s surface temperature less than, or equal to, -90°C&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sentience and sapience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using genetic testing, specimens of SCP-5986 seems to have been around for 500,000 years, if not longer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Log-5986:&lt;/strong&gt; The following is text found in a journal in ███████, Canada. The journal was found in an excavation, unrelated to the foundation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;9th Feb, 1840&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today I found something strange out while hunting. I’m in Canada right? Cold, freezing. Daisies, they’re supposed to grow in warmer places, from what I’ve heard. I wouldn’t know too much would I? But, today I found a daisy! Right here in ███████, a daisy! Well, other than that, not seen nothing strange.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;10th Feb, 1840&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Found more of them daisies. At least 10. I tried to pick one of them, give it to my daughter but the others shot seeds at me like arrows. You believe it? What next, finding sunflowers on the Himilayas?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;11th Feb, 1840&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today I came home with cuts and bruises. Any guesses? Those darn daisies! Kept hitting me ‘til I was forced to retreated. Still stings like mad though. I think I’ll stay well away from hunting now. Maybe kill those things.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by &lt;span class=&quot;printuser avatarhover&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thekidnamedcover&quot;  &gt;&lt;img class=&quot;small&quot; src=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7141604&amp;amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;amp;timestamp=1608694749&quot; alt=&quot;TheKidNamedCover&quot; style=&quot;background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7141604)&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thekidnamedcover&quot;  &gt;TheKidNamedCover&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
